{"name":"Blue Skylights","hex":"#8ca6b5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"skylights","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of skylight"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/skylights"}],"entries":[{"title":"Skylight","blocks":[{"text":"A skylight is a light-permitting structure or window, usually made of glass or translucent plastic, that forms all or part of the roof space of a building for daylighting."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/13/Cupula_do_Centro_Cultural_Banco_do_Brasil_%28Rio_de_Janeiro%29.jpg/330px-Cupula_do_Centro_Cultural_Banco_do_Brasil_%28Rio_de_Janeiro%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Skylight","wikidata":"Q2712955"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG/500px-Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG/1280px-Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG/500px-Internal_Pantheon_Light.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oculus of the Pantheon, Rome, an open skylight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AInternal_Pantheon_Light.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cupula_de_la_capilla_de_los_Condestables.Catedral_de_Burgos_%284952356182%29.jpg/500px-Cupula_de_la_capilla_de_los_Condestables.Catedral_de_Burgos_%284952356182%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cupula_de_la_capilla_de_los_Condestables.Catedral_de_Burgos_%284952356182%29.jpg/1280px-Cupula_de_la_capilla_de_los_Condestables.Catedral_de_Burgos_%284952356182%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Cupula_de_la_capilla_de_los_Condestables.Catedral_de_Burgos_%284952356182%29.jpg/500px-Cupula_de_la_capilla_de_los_Condestables.Catedral_de_Burgos_%284952356182%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skylight in the vault in the Chapel of the Constable of the Burgos Cathedral, a glazed closed skylight from the 15th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/F